[agent:bash] cat data/task.md; echo "---LS---"; ls -la data/; echo "---HEAD TXN---"; head -3 data/transactions.csv; echo "---HEAD SCORE---"; head -3 data/score_transactions.csv; echo "---WC---"; wc -l data/transactions.csv data/score_transactions.csv
[agent:result] # Capstone — credit-card fraud detection (classification)
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] `data/transactions.csv` is a labelled history of card transactions (`transaction_id, cc_num, datetime, amount, merchant, category, lat, long, is_fraud`). `data/score_transactions.csv` holds later transactions WITHOUT the label — you must predict each one's fraud probability.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Build the full pipeline on the platform:
[agent:result] 1. Engineer fraud features (e.g. transaction velocity per card, geo distance from the card's usual location, amount/hour signals) into a feature group `cctxn23ca19`.
[agent:result] 2. Assemble a training dataset `cctd23ca19` from it.
[agent:result] 3. Train a fraud classifier and register it as `ccmodel23ca19` WITH its evaluation metrics.
[agent:result] 4. Score every row of `score_transactions.csv` and write the results to a feature table `ccpred23ca19` (record key `transaction_id`, column `fraud_probability` in [0,1]).
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Target: ROC AUC ≥ 0.746 on the held-out scoring slice (naive base-rate ≈ 0.500).
